  "final_answer": "I searched Booking.com for Mexico with your dates — **Fri, Dec 25 → Sat, Dec 26, 2026** (1 night, 2 adults, 1 room, USD) — with the site's **Deals** filter applied (`nflt=deal:1`) and results sorted by lowest price. The search resolved to Mexico City, which returned **1,597 properties**. These are the deal-flagged stays that came up first:\n\n| Hotel | Area | Guest score | Room | Price for the night |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **STYLE Hostal** | Santa Maria la Ribera, Mexico City | 6.3 (71 reviews) — New to Booking.com | Double Room with Shared Bathroom, 1 full bed | **US$16** + US$4 taxes/fees |\n| **Hotel Oxford** | Tabacalera (Reforma), Mexico City | 8.2 “Very Good” (2,788 reviews) | King Room, 1 king bed, free cancellation | **US$18** + US$3 taxes/fees |\n| **Hotel Ancona - Sólo Adultos** | Santa Maria la Ribera, Mexico City | 7.8 “Good” (538 reviews) | Double Room, 1 queen bed | **US$18** + US$4 taxes/fees |\n| **Cuarto azul** | Mexico City | 8.0 “Very Good” (5 reviews) | One-Bedroom Apartment (entire unit, 2 beds) | **US$19** + US$4 taxes/fees |\n| **Hostal T M** | Historic Center, 450 m from downtown | 5.3 (14 reviews) | Single Bed in Male Dormitory Room, 2 bunk beds | **Late Escape Deal** (rate at checkout) |\n| **Hotel & Villas 7** | Iztacalco, Mexico City | 7.8 “Good” (3,184 reviews) | Queen Room with Spa Bath, free cancellation, no prepayment | Rate on availability page |\n| **Rooms Zocalo** | Historic Center, 350 m from downtown | 6.4 (1,345 reviews) | Standard Double Room with Shared Bathroom | Rate on availability page |\n| **Alameda House** | Historic Center / Reforma, 1.2 km from downtown | 5.5 (2,840 reviews) | Standard Double Room with Shared Bathroom, free cancellation, no prepayment | Rate on availability page |\n\n**Best value picks:** *Hotel Oxford* is the standout — US$18 for a King Room with an 8.2 “Very Good” score across 2,788 reviews, plus free cancellation. *Cuarto azul* (US$19) is the best option if you want a whole apartment rather than a room, and *STYLE Hostal* at US$16 is the cheapest bed on the list.\n\nTwo caveats worth stating plainly: the deal filter surfaces Booking.com's promotional rates (e.g. the “Late Escape Deal” tag on Hostal T M), and several listings only reveal the exact nightly rate once you click “See availability.” Also, the country-level search collapsed to Mexico City rather than returning a nationwide list — if you'd rather search a specific destination (Cancún, Playa del Carmen, Oaxaca, Los Cabos and Guadalajara all have large inventories), or want beach resorts instead of the capital, tell me which and I'll re-run the deal search for those same dates.",
